   <section class="page" data-route="/en/services/energy-modeling" data-page-name="Energy modeling" data-title="Building Energy Modeling in Egypt | eQuest, DesignBuilder">
    <div class="inner-hero max-w-7xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
     <p class="eyebrow">Home / Services / Energy modeling</p>
     <h1>Building Energy Modeling in Egypt: Prove Performance Before You Build</h1>
     <p>A building energy model is a computer simulation that calculates how much energy a building will use, hour by hour, given its shape, envelope, systems, occupancy and climate. WAHDJ builds models in eQuest and DesignBuilder to support design decisions, size mechanical systems and prove compliance for LEED.</p>
     <div class="facts"><strong>In short</strong>
      <p>WAHDJ uses building energy models to compare design options, size systems and document LEED energy performance.</p>
     </div>
    </div>
    <div class="article-copy">
     <h2>When to commission an energy model</h2>
     <h3>Design stage</h3>
     <p>Choose between envelope and system options while changes are still cheap.</p>
     <h3>Compliance</h3>
     <p>LEED energy credits require a comparison between a baseline building and the proposed design. We also provide modeling support for Mostadam compliance where a project requires it.</p>
     <h3>Retrofit</h3>
     <p>Compare measures for an existing building.</p>
     <h2>What you receive</h2>
     <p>Baseline and proposed models, HVAC sizing, measure comparison and a compliance report formatted for the certifying body.</p>
     <h2>The financial logic of modeling</h2>
     <p>The return on modeling comes from the decisions it improves. Right-sized HVAC reduces equipment cost and running cost. The model reports, for each measure, the annual energy saving and the extra cost, so payback can be calculated as extra cost divided by annual saving, using your own tariffs and prices. Savings are validated against utility bills only where operating data exists.</p>
     <h2>Models behind certified and in-progress projects</h2>
     <p><a href="#/en/projects/bureau-58">Bureau 58</a>: LEED Gold, 22,500 m² site. <a href="#/en/projects/credit-agricole">Crédit Agricole Egypt</a>: six certified branches. RCQE Jubail: 20,000 m², in progress; energy modeling.</p>
     <div class="facts"><strong>KEY FACTS</strong>
      <p>Tools: eQuest, DesignBuilder<br>
        Output: baseline versus proposed comparison<br>
        Used for: LEED compliance, HVAC sizing, measure selection</p>
     </div>
